  "recommendation": {
    "word": "hold",
    "why": "The flag is proved to show the original fade and blur on every frame under the WAAPI premises, and every effect it starts meets the Core Animation conditions, with WebKit pixels at grade Q since the compositor blur is not the software blur. It does not cut style or layout passes: the tween still writes the nav on every frame the fade changes, so the recalculation runs anyway, and the Simulator counts of the two arms sit inside the gap between passes. The saving it could bring is paint and raster of the blurred section, which needs a lane with a real GPU. Keep the flag registered, leave it out of the preset, and measure it again together with a variant that also moves the nav write off the main thread."
  }
